TC09 - Verify Footer Community Links Section

Test Steps
Step	Action	Expected Result
1	Open https://playwright.dev/	Playwright homepage is displayed successfully.
2	Scroll down to the footer section of the page.	Footer section is visible.
3	Verify the footer contains a "Community" column/section with links (e.g., Stack Overflow, Discord, Twitter/X).	Community links are visible in the footer.
4	Verify the footer contains a "More" or "Learn" column/section with links (e.g., GitHub, YouTube).	Additional resource links are visible in the footer.
5	Verify the footer contains a copyright notice (e.g., "Copyright © [year] Microsoft").	Copyright text is visible and displays the current year.
6	Click the "Discord" link in the footer (if present).	A new tab opens navigating to the Discord invite/community page.
7	Verify the new tab's URL contains "discord".	URL confirms navigation to the correct external community platform.

Expected Final Result
The user can view all expected footer sections and links, and successfully navigate to an external community platform (Discord) via the footer link.